.TH TERMINAL-ROUTER 1 "September 2026" "terminal-router 1.1.0" "SysLinuxOS Manual"
.SH NAME
terminal\-router \- record tmux terminal sessions for AI\-assisted router work
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B terminal\-router
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B terminal\-router
logs every interactive terminal session to a per\-pane file under
.IR ~/.claude\-logs ,
so an AI assistant such as Claude Code can follow live work on a network device
CLI in real time by reading a single file.
.PP
The intended workflow is an interactive SSH session on a Cisco or Huawei
router. The assistant has no access to the device and never needs any: the
operator types, the assistant reads the log and suggests, the operator decides
what to run.
.PP
All configuration is per\-user and confined to
.IR $HOME .
Nothing is enabled by installing the package; each user must opt in explicitly
and acknowledge the security notice once.
.PP
.B install
and
.B launch
warn, without blocking, if neither
.B claude
nor
.B codex
is found on PATH, since the log they set up then has no AI assistant to
read it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Set up the shell and tmux hooks for the calling user. Idempotent. Logs every
interactive terminal.
.TP
.B launch
Start one self\-contained, one\-off logged tmux session instead. No
.I ~/.bashrc ,
.I ~/.zshrc
or
.I ~/.tmux.conf
edit is made: the hooks are set on that single session only and disappear
with it, so every other terminal \(em Terminator included \(em is
unaffected. Detach with Ctrl\-b d to fall back to a plain shell in the same
window; logging continues while detached. Use pause to suspend capture.
Exiting ends the session.
.TP
.B remove
Undo them. The marked blocks are deleted from
.I ~/.bashrc
and
.IR ~/.tmux.conf ,
both Bash and Zsh startup files are checked, each backed up as
.IR file .terminal\-router.bak ,
the crontab rotation entry is dropped, and the log directory can optionally be
deleted.
.TP
.B status
Report which hooks are active, whether rotation is configured, whether
.B claude
or
.B codex
is on PATH to read the log, how many logs exist and which pane is current.
.TP
.B tail
Follow the newest pane log, switching when the latest symlink changes.
.TP
.B pause
Suspend capture in the calling tmux pane. Also available in launch sessions.
.TP
.B resume
Resume capture in the calling pane into a new file. An already active pipe
is left unchanged.
.TP
.B doctor
Read-only checks for setup, permissions, latest log and live panes. Returns
1 for detected errors and 0 otherwise; warnings alone do not cause failure.
.TP
.B menu
Interactive menu. This is what the desktop entry runs.
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SH SHELL FUNCTIONS
After install, shell shortcuts delegate to the pause and resume commands.
Inside a logged pane,
.B logpause
detaches logging from that pane and
.B logresume
resumes it into a new file. Use them around sensitive work.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc
Marked block that enters tmux on interactive terminals and defines
logpause/logresume. Uses
.I ~/.zshrc
when the login shell is zsh.
.TP
.I ~/.tmux.conf
Marked block with the pipe\-pane hooks.
.TP
.I ~/.claude-logs/
Log directory, mode 0700. Contains one 0600 file per pane and the symlink
.I latest
pointing at the newest.
.TP
.I ~/.config/terminal-router/consent
Records that this user accepted the security notice.
.SH SECURITY
The log captures everything printed in the terminal. Passwords typed at an
interactive prompt (sudo, SSH password authentication) are
.B not
captured, because the tty does not echo them. Secrets that are visible on
screen
.B are
captured: passwords passed as plaintext arguments, tokens in headers, and the
output of
.B cat
on a .env file or a private key. Use
.B logpause
before such work.
.PP
The directory is mode 0700, log files 0600, and a nightly cron job at 03:00
deletes logs older than 30 days.
.SH CAVEATS
Removing the package does not undo the per\-user setup, because dpkg cannot
safely edit every user's home directory. Run
.B terminal\-router remove
before removing the package.
.PP
After upgrading, re-run install to update marked blocks with backups.
Existing tmux servers retain loaded hooks; reload ~/.tmux.conf and use
pause/resume in existing panes to replace old pipes.
.PP
Never run
.B terminal\-router
with sudo: as root it would configure
.I /root
instead of your account, and it refuses to do so.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR crontab (5)
.PP
